{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way","id":1008828,"title":"If the Covenants had their way....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T22:51:09-08:00","id":1008828,"title":"If the Covenants had their way....","content":"So if a Vampire Covenants get's to 'remake' the world with their own image or if they 'won', how different they would be?<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement: Basically a world where Humans and Vampires (along with other supernaturals) coexist or basically a &quot;Communist/Socialist&quot; world under a vampire context. (Although it would be up to humans to overthrow capitalism that the Invictus or Bourgeois Vampires benefit from).<br /> <br /> Invictus: They pretty much want to keep the world as it is now when them ruling from the shadows like the &quot;Vampire Illuminati&quot; sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone: Maybe perhaps a world where Vampires are worshiped as Deities (or act like Faerie folk) who demand blood sacrifices as a exchange for land fertility for crops to grow and such?<br /> <br /> Lancea Et Sanctum: Basically Dark Ages Vampire or a Vampire Theocracy?<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul: Well this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1007021-dracula-the-visionary-and-the-purpose-of-the-ordo-dracul\">thread</a> I've created which is basically the classic &quot;Vampires ruling humans openly like Cattle&quot; scenario which would ultimately resemble the world of Vampire Hunter D...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-27-2016, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:28:14-08:00","id":1008858,"title":"","content":"The Danse Macabre is a supplement in which possibilities are providded for the covenants to be scaled up to globe-spanning conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement calls itself at this scale The Commonwealth. Its goals are: 1) to make cities more accommodating to Kindred unlife; 2) to destroy the differences in material and ;olitical power between neonates and elders; and 3) to undo the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Sanctified call their global organisation The Covenant. They are basically a doomsday-cult, trying to bring about the end of the world in order to force the hand of the forces of good. In the end they want evil to be conquered.<br /> <br /> The Devil's Eye is the Ordo Dracul. They want to create uber vampires, basically. It's not all that different from the regular Ordo.<br /> <br /> Cronies are unified in The Mother's Army. They wish to convert all vampires to their witchy-bitch fest. Second, they want to wake the Crone herself! So that they, three, may learn all of her secrets.<br /> <br /> The Prima Invicta have one simple wish: to rule the world. They're basically the NWO, cleaned out of its anti-semetic descriptors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:57:55-08:00","id":1009041,"title":"","content":"The Carthians get scarier as an organization the higher they get to step up the scale of their ambitions. If you go by the conspiracy descriptions in the Danse Macabre, the Carthians, not the Ordo, are the ones most likely to plan out a bizarre dystopia with humans ruled like cattle. It may not be their first choice, but the repeated watchword is a reminder that when Carthians say they want the proletariat to seize the means of production from the bourgeoisie, the living are not the proletariat they're talking about. The living are the <i>means of production</i> to be seized and distributed.<br /> <br /> The Ordo, meanwhile, don't really have as much of an organizational thrust on this level; their ideology is individualistic, and they exist as an organization mostly as a support group for their members to realize that ideology for themselves. A Dragon, given his apocalyptic druthers, would probably become some manner of terrifying, tyrannical blood god, but most of them probably aren't much invested the idea of their fellow Dragons becoming divine peers.<br /> <br /> Your idea for the Acolytes sounds about right to me. A fallen Masquerade and scattered Kindred across the world, taking roles as local Merlins and holy patrons to be appeased and supplicated, at once apart from their communities but connected to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:46:30-08:00","id":1009056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009041#post1009041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Carthians get scarier as an organization the higher they get to step up the scale of their ambitions. If you go by the conspiracy descriptions in the Danse Macabre, the Carthians, not the Ordo, are the ones most likely to plan out a bizarre dystopia with humans ruled like cattle. It may not be their first choice, but the repeated watchword is a reminder that when Carthians say they want the proletariat to seize the means of production from the bourgeoisie, the living are not the proletariat they're talking about. The living are the <i>means of production</i> to be seized and distributed.<br /> <br /> The Ordo, meanwhile, don't really have as much of an organizational thrust on this level; their ideology is individualistic, and they exist as an organization mostly as a support group for their members to realize that ideology for themselves. A Dragon, given his apocalyptic druthers, would probably become some manner of terrifying, tyrannical blood god, but most of them probably aren't much invested the idea of their fellow Dragons becoming divine peers.<br /> <br /> Your idea for the Acolytes sounds about right to me. A fallen Masquerade and scattered Kindred across the world, taking roles as local Merlins and holy patrons to be appeased and supplicated, at once apart from their communities but connected to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all of this undermines what i originally have in mind, and plus the whole &quot;Ruling Humanity as Cattle&quot; is actually antithetical to Marxist/Communist ideology since it's really supposed to be a classless society which humans are included as well. I think a more accurate version of what a Carthian world would look like would be similar to True Blood under the vampire context but however though, they'll leave it up to humans to overthrow their own oppressive system being capitalism which only then the Carthian goal would be complete (at least how I imagine it).<br /> <br /> The reason I've placed the &quot;Ruling Humans like Cattle&quot; into the Ordo Dracul is because each Vampire is able to be their own tyrannical blood god, ruling humanity in their own individualistic castles with 'villages' below or at least how the world is like in &quot;Vampire Hunter D&quot; or basically each Vampire are basically the &quot;Nobility&quot; that hold titles like &quot;Count/Countess&quot; &quot;Baron/Baroness&quot; &quot;Lord/Duchess&quot;, etc which mirrors a twisted version of Feudalism or Aristocracy (or basically every Vampires are members of a vast Aristocracy) or at least this is what how I imagine Dracula himself would model his ideal society from while taking the Baroque/Victorian aesthetic along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-27-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:54:28-08:00","id":1009057,"title":"","content":"I do think, mind, that a lot of Carthians would agree with you and feel kinship with living humans in their cause of a just and proper society. The Carthians are very far from monolithic and probably the most ideologically diverse of the five core covenants. I imagine they have a lot of infighting between members with incompatible philosophies of social rule.<br /> <br /> Their danger, organizationally, is that they're susceptible to cults of personality and charismatic ideologues: because they're open to wide swaths of new ideas and take passionate ethical stands, Carthians radicalize easily. When you give the Movement sufficient numbers and resources to enact massive world-changing policies, conditions are ideal for a few mad firebrands to take things completely off the rails, one step at a time. That's how you end up with visions like the Commonwealth. It's also, I imagine, how you'd end up splintering the covenant, with a large minority of Carthians opposed to the new face of the Movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T15:50:34-08:00","id":1009072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009056#post1009056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all of this undermines what i originally have in mind, and plus the whole &amp;quot;Ruling Humanity as Cattle&amp;quot; is actually antithetical to Marxist/Communist ideology since it's really supposed to be a classless society which humans are included as well. I think a more accurate version of what a Carthian world would look like would be similar to True Blood under the vampire context but however though, they'll leave it up to humans to overthrow their own oppressive system being capitalism which only then the Carthian goal would be complete (at least how I imagine it).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Carthians aren't just a Covenant of Marxists and communists. The ideologies encompassed by the Carthian movement are many and varied - everything from anarchism to fascism. The only thing they have in common is that they oppose the Invictus' way of doing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T17:00:44-08:00","id":1009088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009056#post1009056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think all of this undermines what i originally have in mind, and plus the whole &quot;Ruling Humanity as Cattle&quot; is actually antithetical to Marxist/Communist ideology since it's really supposed to be a classless society which humans are included as well. I think a more accurate version of what a Carthian world would look like would be similar to True Blood under the vampire context but however though, they'll leave it up to humans to overthrow their own oppressive system being capitalism which only then the Carthian goal would be complete (at least how I imagine it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Carthians are socialist though, Jannol. The New Wave Requiem source book mentions that there were a large number of capitalist democratic firebrands in the 80s and fascist firebrands have existed too. The Carthains are ultimately a group that rejects the feudalism of the Invictus in favor of adopting a more modern style of government inspired by mortal systems, though different carthains have different ideas on what that system should be, an individual firebrand could be a socialist, a neoliberal, a fascist or literally any other ideology that isn't feudalism.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I think you are right about how a socialist Carthain would see their ideal society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:48:12-08:00","id":1009118,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm sure of, whoever wins, we're screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:48:22-08:00","id":1009151,"title":"","content":"Boiling them down, Carthians are the ones trying to pretend they're still human, by attributing human social structures to vampire societies. Carthians winning would just lead to them living alongside humanity, and likely eventually turning into the sort of tyranny you would see if the Invictus won, or some sort of wickedly depraved blood capitalism.<br /> <br /> Howalt had a good point, they call them 'gonzo' covenants in the Danse Macabre but they are sort of super-empowered versions of the existing ones. The Circle of the Crone one is called the Mother's Army, and there is a definite Crone who speaks to them through their blood and who all members are attuned to. Such a thing would be a huge win to a pagan group who otherwise is as anchored by faith as the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum were a doomsday cult, which fits. Once you've converted everyone you would either exist solely to be tempter, tormentor and executioner, or try to hurry along Judgment Day so that you can finally get that reward you believe in. Of course one could argue the former would lead to the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:18:06-08:00","id":1009164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009118#post1009118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm sure of, whoever wins, we're screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's the number one reason to go unaligned and say &quot;Fuck them All&quot; even though using things that you gained from them (like Coils, Cruac, etc) when you were once a member to your own advantage .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:18:30-08:00","id":1009184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009164#post1009164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe that's the number one reason to go unaligned and say &quot;Fuck them All&quot; even though using things that you gained from them (like Coils, Cruac, etc) when you were once a member to your own advantage .</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:43:29-08:00","id":1009204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009184#post1009184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking about mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was referring to if any Kindred had any compassion towards mortals and sees them more than just a food source or cattle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:03:09-08:00","id":1009356,"title":"","content":"Outside of the Ordo Dracul, most groups will need loyalist humans of some sort, ghouls or not. Being unable to act fully during the day would be a huge disadvantage in ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:28:40-08:00","id":1009429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009056#post1009056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all of this undermines what i originally have in mind, and plus the whole &quot;Ruling Humanity as Cattle&quot; is actually antithetical to Marxist/Communist ideology since it's really supposed to be a classless society which humans are included as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Marxist/Communist a society of the undead humans aren't a class, they're part of the means of production. To break it down further, humans are a subject of labor, they're raw materials to be owned collectively not equal partners. Elder, and/or low humanity, Carthians probably don't view humans as much more than the raw materials over which kindred fight. Younger, or more humane, Carthians might want to see a more a egalitarian solution.<br /> <br /> Any human ideology the Carthians adapt needs to account for the fact that kindred existence is based on predation of sentient beings. If vampires have a right to exist, then they have a right to feed, which means humans aren't an equal part in any utopian society the Carthians might dream up. Debating how to accommodate this probably takes up a lot of time in the Carthian movement, and leads to splinter upon splinter upon splinter of ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:00:56-08:00","id":1009499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009429#post1009429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a Marxist/Communist a society of the undead humans aren't a class, they're part of the means of production. To break it down further, humans are a subject of labor, they're raw materials to be owned collectively not equal partners. Elder, and/or low humanity, Carthians probably don't view humans as much more than the raw materials over which kindred fight. Younger, or more humane, Carthians might want to see a more a egalitarian solution.<br /> <br /> Any human ideology the Carthians adapt needs to account for the fact that kindred existence is based on predation of sentient beings. If vampires have a right to exist, then they have a right to feed, which means humans aren't an equal part in any utopian society the Carthians might dream up. Debating how to accommodate this probably takes up a lot of time in the Carthian movement, and leads to splinter upon splinter upon splinter of ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually reminds me of the strawman arguments used against communism for example the whole &quot;Community of Women&quot; where bourgeois critics fear that women were part of the means of production to be freely passed around men even though what Marx was actually describing is abolishing the patriarchal family system altogether and yet things like this treat strawman arguments as reality which is a bad track record for WW at times (for example, the Black Furry backstory is based on the whole &quot;False Rape accusation&quot; trope as I heard).<br /> <br /> (Assuming this if this is what WW has written into the books about the Carthians)<br /> <br /> Realistically, in order for a Communist society to work then Vampires regarding Humans as equal partners is pretty much required especially due to the reason that Humans are simply what they once were and they need to respect that and see them as more than just food sources which empathy is actually key to Leftist thinking. Anything on the contrary becomes either capitalism or any form of class society that is even more monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-28-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:57:23-08:00","id":1009525,"title":"","content":"I'm loving this discussion.<br /> <br /> Vein, you seem to be looking at the Carthians as human. They're vampires. They prey on people. It's necessary for their existence. Holding on to a view that there's an equality between them and humanity is one for the young and naive. How many people can you kill before you finally have to accept &quot;I am more important than them, as a species&quot;. Humans, gradually, become to them as animals do to us. Food. Talking food. <br /> <br /> <br /> Any discussion of the future of a Carthian state should consider Animal Farm as a model IMO. The Carthians would have noble ideals, but end up pigs. Power corrupts; and Vampires are inherently selfish individuals by their very nature. There's no way noble ideology lasts, under them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:44:00-08:00","id":1009543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009525#post1009525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving this discussion.<br /> <br /> Vein, you seem to be looking at the Carthians as human. They're vampires. They prey on people. It's necessary for their existence. Holding on to a view that there's an equality between them and humanity is one for the young and naive. How many people can you kill before you finally have to accept &quot;I am more important than them, as a species&quot;. Humans, gradually, become to them as animals do to us. Food. Talking food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, Vampires used to be Human before they were embraced which is common courtesy to see humans as more than just food sources but also as equal partners which is actually the entire humanity system is about isn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009525#post1009525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any discussion of the future of a Carthian state should consider Animal Farm as a model IMO. The Carthians would have noble ideals, but end up pigs. Power corrupts; and Vampires are inherently selfish individuals by their very nature. There's no way noble ideology lasts, under them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double Facepalm...<br /> <br /> Here we go with the liberal tirades again with the &quot;Appeal to Nature&quot; (the &quot;Human Nature&quot; argument) fallacies which has Christian roots of the &quot;Divine Right of Kings&quot; and the &quot;Original Sin&quot; concluding that all humans (and vampires as we're discussing here) are all irredeemably evil which is also where the &quot;power corrupts&quot; narratives come from.<br /> <br /> Also you overlook the fact that George Orwell's &quot;Animal Farm&quot; was nothing but a polemic against the Soviet Union which it's socialism/communism never developed properly because of Capitalism sabotaging it and among other reasons that Russia wasn't a fully industrialized country (since Marx originally wanted to have the revolution to happen in more industrialized nations like Germany, France and Britain before Russia) which later became a &quot;Non-Society&quot; that was about to collapse which it did and it became capitalist as it is today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-28-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:57:31-08:00","id":1009577,"title":"","content":"It's quite a leap to say &quot;<i>empathy is actually key to Leftist thinking</i>&quot; when such a statement is handily disproved by every human fasc/com who has ever come to power throughout history. Then you add undead, immortal monsters to the equation and I wonder if the death toll from a Kindred com/fasc leader would surpass that of the historic human ones?<br /> <br /> You may say that a pet is part of your family but when push comes to shove, it's life is never as valuable as any human member of said family and since vampires prey on humans as we do on animals, I would expect the relationship to be similar.<br /> <br /> Carthians have the fewest Elders of any Covenant but I would expect them to be as different from the starry eyed Neonates without a trove (un)life experience as the human leader of any far Leftist nation is from the plebs over which he rules. As with any ideology, the utopia falls apart when it collides with human nature. With vampiric nature being inherently different from our own, I'm sure it would be even more difficult to build any longstanding utopia than it is for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 11-28-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:47:02-08:00","id":1009587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009577#post1009577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's quite a leap to say &quot;<i>empathy is actually key to Leftist thinking</i>&quot; when such a statement is handily disproved by every human fasc/com who has ever come to power throughout history. Then you add undead, immortal monsters to the equation and I wonder if the death toll from a Kindred com/fasc leader would surpass that of the historic human ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we go again with the liberalism citing 'history' as &quot;proof&quot; to justify &quot;muh horseshoe&quot; theory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009577#post1009577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may say that a pet is part of your family but when push comes to shove, it's life is never as valuable as any human member of said family and since vampires prey on humans as we do on animals, I would expect the relationship to be similar.<br /> <br /> Carthians have the fewest Elders of any Covenant but I would expect them to be as different from the starry eyed Neonates without a trove (un)life experience as the human leader of any far Leftist nation is from the plebs over which he rules. As with any ideology, the utopia falls apart when it collides with human nature. With vampiric nature being inherently different from our own, I'm sure it would be even more difficult to build any longstanding utopia than it is for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only except humans are not animals at all which is the major difference.<br /> <br /> Which once again here's even more &quot;inherit nature&quot; arguments once again.<br /> <br /> Looks like this thread is getting derailed by the inherit liberalism here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-28-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:57:44-08:00","id":1009591,"title":"","content":"I'd typed out a thought-out response to you, but after your reply to Rathamus I figured why bother.<br /> <br /> Find it pretty hilarious that you're on a rant about liberalism, when your view is &quot;it's common courtesy [for vampires] to see humans as equal partners&quot;. That is so ridiculously liberal and naive it hurts.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a shame you are derailing the thread with a bizarre (and misguided) rant about liberalism, when others where making cogent points about the reality of a vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:04:31-08:00","id":1009593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009591#post1009591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find it pretty hilarious that you're on a rant about liberalism, when your view is &quot;it's common courtesy [for vampires] to see humans as equal partners&quot;. That is so ridiculously liberal and naive it hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you know what Liberalism actually means....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-29-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:20:46-08:00","id":1009596,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna interject my two cents if you don't mind. Now, from what I gather people become more jaded and less idealistic the older they get. Now, what helps keep society itself from falling apart from all the cynicism is the fact that humans eventually die. Vampires have a shot at eternal life if they play their cards right; sure, this supposed vampire and human utopia might start out just like that (unlikely, but that's beside the point). The human aspect would as a whole still be idealistic, but the vampire aspect would slowly lose it's ideals and end up like Stalinist Russia. I think the thought boils down to that at the end of the night, we are still their food. Sure, we are somewhat intelligent food and we have our uses, but at the end of the night we are food nonetheless. I doubt that the all night society is going to respect its food enough to keep a human/vampire utopia as a utopia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T23:59:27-08:00","id":1009656,"title":"","content":"Your ideas of Carthians could work, Veindark. If and only if the vast majority of them would be able to maintain a Humanity of 5+. Lower than 7, you don't mind injuring someone over blood. Lower than 6, you don't mind eating a child. In other words, at 5 people have effectively become cattle to you. Seeing as many players have no problem with impassionate violence (sin agains Humanity 4), it's not at all unreasonable to assume that it is highly unlikely for the vast majority of vampires to remain at a higher Humanity than 5. Which would be required for your version of Carthian utopia. I think most stabilize around 4-5.<br /> <br /> The human Veindark might not believe humans are animals, but the fact is he's wrong according to the 200 year old vampire Darwin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:37:21-08:00","id":1009665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009593#post1009593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like you know what Liberalism actually means....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Took you 3 hours, after originally posting, to completely change your reply. <br /> Looks like you don't know what you mean, period. <br /> <br /> Go find a politics forum somewhere. The rest of us are talking about vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:11:16-08:00","id":1009670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009587#post1009587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">humans are not animals at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... I hate to break it to you, but this is just factually inaccurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:20:19-08:00","id":1009677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009670#post1009670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... I hate to break it to you, but this is just factually inaccurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to reply the same, with the caveat that for the purposes of an ideology like Humanity, there might be a real difference. Buuuuuut I was looking at the posts in question and realizing it may just fall on deaf ears. The rest of this thread is interesting, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:37:16-08:00","id":1009686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009656#post1009656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human Veindark might not believe humans are animals, but the fact is he's wrong according to the 200 year old vampire Darwin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instant inspiration:<br /> <br /> &quot;I met Darwin, and he most certainly did not sound like that. No, no, I don't mean 'I'm old enough as a vampire to have known him in my youth.' I mean that I saw him last year. Met him walking along the beach. I'd heard the rumors, that he was in the area. It wasn't the first time I'd heard them, but those stories are as much a fantasy to our kind as our kind are to the kine. And yet I am wooing some bronzed young thing on the beach under the midnight sun, all set to satisfy <i>multiple </i>hungers, and then he is there. She spooks, of course, but I don't blame her. <i>I </i>spooked. One moment, it's just us, and in the next instant he's there. I didn't see how he approached. Sea birds, maybe a crab, hell, I don't know. Maybe he was just in the water.<br /> <br /> &quot;Because, you see, with Darwin, that's just it. He tells me of his long journey amid the ocean's life, resting during the day down where the sun cannot reach, taking the form of fanged predators to consume prey. How he can still subsist on animals I don't know. No one does. He's wandered for a couple hundred years now. You know, and I never asked, but he starts telling me of this grand journey. 'From breath to blood to brethren, I will have known them all,' he says, in the most grandiose voice you can imagine. I'd have laughed in his stiff old face if he wasn't so intense about it. You believe him. Trust me. He says that he's taken the forms of more animals than the number people I've met in my lifetime \u2014 <i>un</i>lifetime included. All part of the greatest experiment. To experience his own evolution through taking part in that whole 'red in tooth and claw' thing. I mean, really taking part. Taking them apart.<br /> <br /> &quot;And you know, it wasn't that he was hostile. Far from it. He seemed completely indifferent to my anger. I could feel his power. He's old, yes, but he's seen things none of us can imagine. Who knows what horrific shape he might take on, all parts of the million different things he's eaten? [shivers] I don't even want to try it. And if you ever meet him, or hear the rumors that he's around, I'd advise you to believe them. Be careful. You don't know if that fly you're going to swat, or that cat you're going to ghoul, or that dog that is watching you <i>really </i>closely, is just an animal. Best to keep your wits about you. Stay observant. Watch the natural world for the supernatural. You'll feel a lot safer for it.<br /> <br /> &quot;The thing is, I think that's what Darwin wants. You get to live a little in his world when you pay attention to those things. Maybe it makes you a better vampire. Maybe it just makes you paranoid. Either way, it's going to change you, and change, my friend, is evolution of a sort. I've never been much of a scientist myself, not much of a reader, but I can tell you this: I eagerly await the follow-up volume to <i>On the Origin of Species </i>once he completes whatever journey he's on!&quot;<br /> <br /> (Darwin must totally be a Gangrel, and I'm guessing Ordo Dracul fits best!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 11-29-2016, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T02:20:53-08:00","id":1009696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009577#post1009577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's quite a leap to say &quot;<i>empathy is actually key to Leftist thinking</i>&quot; when such a statement is handily disproved by every human fasc/com who has ever come to power throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to add another perspective since I believe most people in this thread right now comes from the US. Historically socialism and communism hasn't worked out great, but in modern days socialist parties are the most empathetic and progressive parties all over Europe.<br /> In fact, I live in a country where the Social Democrats party has historically been the most progressive and empathic party since it was founded over a hundred years ago. Recently the even more leftist Left Party has taken over that role after an ideological shift from communism to socialism and social democracy.<br /> The largest liberal party, the Moderates, have quite a different history with voting against women's suffrage, openly supporting Apartheid in South Africa, and postponing the decision to appeal compulsory sterilization of trans people (that happened 2012). Today there is a small (but not marginally so) movement inside the party who wants to openly cooperate with the neo-nazi party just to increase the chance of them being able to form government after the next election.<br /> <br /> So while I'm perfectly aware that more people died under Stalin than under Hitler, the fact is that socialists has always been the most empathetic people in Sweden since Sweden became a democracy.<br /> <br /> I'm not very invested in this particular thread, but I needed to show people how it looks today outside the history books and outside the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:31:59-08:00","id":1009707,"title":"","content":"I love you, Claire Redfield.<br /> <br /> You make him out to be this great candidate for a version of Golgonda I've been toying with in my mind: transcendence understood as resuming to be a part of the natural order of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:46:56-08:00","id":1009808,"title":"","content":"Jannol/Veindark, I Pmd you about this conversation, but it comes down to VtR vampires kind of being bastards who can turn any ideology, no matter how good that ideology is amoung humans, into something abusive and twisted. The invictus are the establishment as run by bastards, the Lance is Christianity as run by bastards, the Circle of the Crone is paganism as run by bastards and the Ordo is science as run by bastards. And the Carthans are revolutionary movements, including socialist movements, as run by bastards.<br /> <br /> and just because everyone is saying the Carthains would probably twist socialism into something ugly doesn't mean that they oppose socialism IRL, it just means that they recognize that VtR vamps, being bastards, could twist it the way that can and do twist every ideology into something ugly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:54:45-08:00","id":1009814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009808#post1009808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jannol/Veindark, I Pmd you about this conversation, but it comes down to VtR vampires kind of being bastards who can turn any ideology, no matter how good that ideology is amoung humans, into something abusive and twisted. The invictus are the establishment as run by bastards, the Lance is Christianity as run by bastards, the Circle of the Crone is paganism as run by bastards and the Ordo is science as run by bastards. And the Carthans are revolutionary movements, including socialist movements, as run by bastards.<br /> <br /> and just because everyone is saying the Carthains would probably twist socialism into something ugly doesn't mean that they oppose socialism IRL, it just means that they recognize that VtR vamps, being bastards, could twist it the way that can and do twist every ideology into something ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> In the game I hope to run soon, the Carthians seized control of the city and started out with utopian ideals and all turned out to be bastards, including screwing over other Carthians. While their overt politics are comparable to my own politics (I am pretty far left) I didn't really see how a utopian Carthian domain would work because vampires ruin everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:59:42-08:00","id":1009905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009814#post1009814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...vampires ruin everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little known fact, that's the official tourism slogan of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:03:59-08:00","id":1010318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008828-if-the-covenants-had-their-way?p=1009814#post1009814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly.<br /> <br /> In the game I hope to run soon, the Carthians seized control of the city and started out with utopian ideals and all turned out to be bastards, including screwing over other Carthians. While their overt politics are comparable to my own politics (I am pretty far left) I didn't really see how a utopian Carthian domain would work because vampires ruin everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think in order to run a truly great City, you need to be sympathetic to the ideologies of the people in charge, and then also understand the complaints against those ideologies in order to make them monsters. Someone who wants to run a Carthian controlled city needs to get the underlying reasons they are supported, and then make their eventual victory/truth behind the mask exactly what people who don't like Carthian politics expect. The same should happen with whatever Covenant is in charge, which is why I'll never be making a Circle lead city. I don't connect with them enough to do them justice like that. (Will revisit the Circle stance after Secrets of the Covenants comes out, but I'm not hopeful and it is entirely a me issue.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}